{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375722-bitter-fury-soulsteel-reaper-daiklaive-peach","id":1375722,"title":"Bitter Fury (Soulsteel Reaper Daiklaive) [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-19T17:45:10-07:00","id":1375722,"title":"Bitter Fury (Soulsteel Reaper Daiklaive) [PEACH]","content":"A player had an idea for an artifact for their character that'll be joining my Western game, and while they had a core concept they wanted they gave me pretty much free reign to flesh it out as I saw fit. This is the result so far!<br /> <br /> Couple things.<br /> First, yes, these are mostly reskinned and tweaked Dragonblooded charms. My brain am dumb at creating mechanics so it's much, much easier for me to build off of an existing framework.<br /> Second, the description wasn't originally full of impenetrable Japanese terminology. I was just using the terms for things that were specific to a Japanese sword and then a friend challenged me to do full weeb and make it as dense and absurd as I reasonably could.<br /> <br /> Here's the pitch I was given by the player.<br /> &quot;His father was a Fire Aspect Magistrate. Who faced down and lost to an Abyssal called the Dark Maker, who subsequently hammered his soul into a soulsteel flame-blade. The character vowed revenge and infiltrated the Abyssal's manse and sought to slay him at the seemingly certain cost of his own life. He cought the notice of the Unconquered Sun, defeated his opponent and recovered the weapon, which now now speaks to and advises the character, urging him to use his skills for infiltration toward justice. Today the character is a wandering mandalorian-esque bounty hunter. Trying to live up to his father's name whilst living in the shadows.&quot;<br /> <br /> And here's the result! <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bitter Fury</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Soulsteel Reaper Daiklaive - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attunement</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> 5m</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Medium (+3 Acc, +10 Dmg, +1 Def, Ovw 4)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Lethal, Melee, Balanced</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hearthstone Slot(s)</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> 1</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Era</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Time of Tumult</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Setting sail from Skullstone, the Abyssal craftsman known simply as the Dark Maker prowled the western oceans, hunting for ruins and wreckage from the lost First Age. During once such endeavor the death knight\u2019s fleet discovered a lost Peleps vessel, long separated from their armada by the wrath of a Storm Mother. Starved and thirsty, the crew fell prey to the Dark Maker with relative ease, increasing the Abyssal\u2019s crew with each man that fell. The crew fell easily, that is, save for one. A valiant Fire Aspect fought tooth and nail at first to drive off the invaders, and once that cause was clearly lost, he battled to deny the brigands the spoils by sinking the very ship he battled on. His efforts, sadly, were for naught. The crew slain, the ship taken, the brave Prince of Creation was taken prisoner.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Dark Maker returned to his hidden workshop, a manse corrupted by the dark essence of the shadowland that overtook it, with his spoils in tow. There he questioned the Fire Aspect with tortures both mundane and mystical for the knowledge of the Peleps navy\u2019s movements. No matter the horrors inflicted, however, the man would not break. Frustrated but refusing to walk away without another prize, the Death Knight murdered the loyal Peleps soldier, smelting his soul and the souls of his crew with underworld iron in the cold flames of his balefire crucible. Working day and night without sleep or sustenance, ensuring that no light other than the heatless sun of the underworld or the green balefire of the forge touched the iron, the Dark Maker fashioned an elegant reaper daiklaive from the resulting soulsteel. The rage of Hesiesh is not so easily quenched, however, and the divine spark of the dragons had an unexpected effect on the blade. Re-entering creation, basking in the warmth of the Unconquered Sun\u2019s light, the embers of the souls forged into the steel began to reignite, hungering for vengeance against the dark beings that trapped them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bitter Fury is an elegant, almost impossibly thin soulsteel reaper daiklaive. As further insult to the souls trapped within, its habaki and kashira are crafted from Malfean brass and the iron tsuba is carved in the shape of dragons bound in barbed chains. The same-kawa is fashioned from the skin of strange creatures fished from the depths of the underworld\u2019s seas, the tsuka-ito is woven from the hair of dead sailors, and the mekugi that holds the whole blade together is carved from the Dragonblood\u2019s finger bone. The pained faces indicative of soulsteel aren't visible in the hiraji, the metal instead appearing as a matte black void. With close inspection the faces are visible in the hamon, warped into silent screams of rage rather than pain, and they glow faintly as if the metal hasn\u2019t fully cooled when the blade is drawn in Creation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Evocations of Bitter Fury</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fire Aspect Dragonblooded are always resonant with this artifact as the Exalted essence trapped within knows its own.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When attuning themselves to Bitter Fury, the Exalt can accept the Major intimacy \u201cAnathema (Hatred)\u201d to awaken Hate\u2019s Razor Edge at no cost. This intimacy cannot be reduced or increased in any way while the artifact is attuned, and while the Exalt is aware that the intimacy is not entirely their own, it functions for all intents and purposes as if it were. The Exalt can either purchase or re-purchase the evocation at standard cost to overcome the furious souls\u2019 will, either waiving or removing the intimacy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Hate\u2019s Razor Edge</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Decisive-only, Resonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Channeling the rage of hte souls trapped within, Bitter Fury\u2019s edge cuts through armor as though it were ice. She ignores (Strength/2, rounded up) points of Hardness, plus an additional point for every 10 on her attack roll. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> An Exalt resonant with Bitter Fury doubles the Hardness ignored and inflicts aggravated damage against Creatures of Darkness or beings targeted by the weapon\u2019s ingrained intimacy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vengeance\u2019s Radiance</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Resonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> One scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whipping the trapped souls into a frenzy, the faces running the edge of the blade glow like coals stoked to roar a forge back to life. The weapon gains +1 Overwhelming and an enemy damaged by a decisive attack takes a -1 wound penalty until the end of his next turn as their nerves scream at the impossible heat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For an additional 2m and 1w, Bitter Fury inflicts aggravated damage against Creatures of Darkness or beings targeted by the weapon\u2019s ingrained intimacy for the duration of this evocation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fury Knows No Bounds</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4m; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Dual, Resonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Hate\u2019s Razor Edge, Vengeance\u2019s Radiance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once a warrior is this familiar with the blade and those that reside within, they can strike out at a distance. The Exalt makes a withering or decisive attack with (Dexterity + [Archery, Thrown, Melee, or an appropriate Martial Art]) against an enemy within short range. This attack deals lethal damage. Withering attacks have a damage of 10 + Essence, not adding strength. Decisive attacks double 10s on damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This attack counts as a Flame weapon for any charms that make use of them.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 03-20-2020, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T02:41:57-07:00","id":1375776,"title":"","content":"You're missing the Resonant Keyword on the Charms.<br /> <br /> Fury Knows No Bounds is a little weird. It's a Reaper Daiklave Flame weapon I can use with Thrown or Archery but not Single Point or Righteous Devil? I'd either pair the ranged attack down to a standard Dex+Melee roll, or open it to all combat abilities.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks great. 3-dots.<br /> <br /> I'd strongly consider looking at Asphodel and cribbing out some of the ghostly mentor shtick to make this feel more &quot;Soulsteel-y&quot; (and meet player expectations), but nix the Shadow-World stuff. If front-loaded (like Asphodel) then 4 dots. If it needs to be unlocked (like Daring Venture), then 3-dots.<br /> <br /> Really cool artifact. I'm very impressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T06:48:15-07:00","id":1375799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375722-bitter-fury-soulsteel-reaper-daiklaive-peach?p=1375776#post1375776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing the Resonant Keyword on the Charms.<br /> <br /> Fury Knows No Bounds is a little weird. It's a Reaper Daiklave Flame weapon I can use with Thrown or Archery but not Single Point or Righteous Devil? I'd either pair the ranged attack down to a standard Dex+Melee roll, or open it to all combat abilities.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks great. 3-dots.<br /> <br /> I'd strongly consider looking at Asphodel and cribbing out some of the ghostly mentor shtick to make this feel more &amp;quot;Soulsteel-y&amp;quot; (and meet player expectations), but nix the Shadow-World stuff. If front-loaded (like Asphodel) then 4 dots. If it needs to be unlocked (like Daring Venture), then 3-dots.<br /> <br /> Really cool artifact. I'm very impressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonant: Derp. Brain am dumb. Easy enough to fix.<br /> <br /> Fury Knows No Bounds: I did intend for it to play nice with Righteous Devil, which is why I added the &quot;this counts as a flame weapon&quot; but that only helps my players. Is there a better way you can think of to word that that makes it more readily apparent?<br /> Asphodel: OH holy shit, yes. That absolutely is something I want to incorporate! I let the player take a 1 dot mentor that'd be narratively work a bit more like Whispers in 1e and 2e (you don't actually talk to the weapon, but there is a level of intuitive communication.) Looks like I know what I'm reading on break later<br /> <br /> Thanks for the input and I'm really glad someone thinks it might be almost as neat as it is in my head!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T07:16:05-07:00","id":1375803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375722-bitter-fury-soulsteel-reaper-daiklaive-peach?p=1375799#post1375799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fury Knows No Bounds: I did intend for it to play nice with Righteous Devil, which is why I added the &amp;quot;this counts as a flame weapon&amp;quot; but that only helps my players. Is there a better way you can think of to word that that makes it more readily apparent?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Exalt makes a withering or decisive attack with (Dexterity + [Archery, Thrown, or Melee])&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't use Righteous Devil Charms with Archery, Melee or Thrown.<br /> <br /> I suggest something like: &quot;The Exalt makes a withering or decisive attack with (Dexterity + [Archery, Thrown, Melee or an appropriate Martial Art])&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T08:43:29-07:00","id":1375817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375722-bitter-fury-soulsteel-reaper-daiklaive-peach?p=1375803#post1375803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;The Exalt makes a withering or decisive attack with (Dexterity + [Archery, Thrown, or Melee])&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> You can't use Righteous Devil Charms with Archery, Melee or Thrown.<br /> <br /> I suggest something like: &amp;quot;The Exalt makes a withering or decisive attack with (Dexterity + [Archery, Thrown, Melee or an appropriate Martial Art])&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaaand fixed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T17:45:57-07:00","id":1376340,"title":"","content":"I rather like the sword, I think it's well done.<br /> <br /> I do have one question- there's an odd interaction in Hate's Razor Edge. Because you half strength then round up, for example, a Strength 3 character will ignore 2 points of Hardness. With resonant benefits, they actually ignore more than their Strength, they ignore 4, since the hardness to be ignored is what doubles. I don't think this is exactly broken, it still caps at about 6 hardness ignored, however it is a curious quirk of the phrasing of both elements. Was it intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/655-senara","name":"Senara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar655_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T22:18:15-07:00","id":1376371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Senara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1375722-bitter-fury-soulsteel-reaper-daiklaive-peach?p=1376340#post1376340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather like the sword, I think it's well done.<br /> <br /> I do have one question- there's an odd interaction in Hate's Razor Edge. Because you half strength then round up, for example, a Strength 3 character will ignore 2 points of Hardness. With resonant benefits, they actually ignore more than their Strength, they ignore 4, since the hardness to be ignored is what doubles. I don't think this is exactly broken, it still caps at about 6 hardness ignored, however it is a curious quirk of the phrasing of both elements. Was it intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the bits cribbed straight from DB (Burning Fury Wreath, WFHW pg 225)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}